The 4 October 2026 support export records reports merged into #4471. The existing
[incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls them one month-first parser issue. Tenant locale,
booking form, and report channel show two causes. This page records the split against that
export; new reports need a fresh count.

<IncidentSplit ticket={4471} />

## Problem 1 · shared parser

The shared parser reads dates month first. People at day-first tenants enter dates day first,
so ambiguous dates can change month and day. This affects reports from the app and email,
and reports from the `booking-v2` form. Example: R-41200 describes 7 April becoming 4 July
at Harbour Dental (`en-GB`, `booking-v2`). Fix the parser according to the tenant's locale
and test ambiguous dates across the affected channels.

## Problem 2 · booking-v3 hint

The `booking-v3` form displays `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants. People follow that hint,
but the form reads the entered date in the tenant's day-first order. Example: R-41230
describes 6 January becoming 1 June at Copper Studio (`es-ES`, `booking-v3`, form channel).
Make the hint and form interpretation agree with the tenant's locale; test the form path
separately from the shared parser.

<Callout>
The two problems share symptoms and subject lines. The browser's intake tag is a guess;
do not use it or the subject as the cause. Count each report ID once, then use the tenant
directory, locale, booking form, and channel to place it.
</Callout>

## Triage and follow-up

Keep one engineering ticket per cause. Reports in `desk-notes.json` described as
one-day moves remain in the parser group under the existing tenant-based rule. Recheck their
individual evidence if a later investigation establishes another cause.

The [subject-only triage rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) and [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
are historical records of why the desk merged these reports. A new decision should replace
that rule if the desk adopts cause-based merging; do not edit the accepted decision in place.

